{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Problem and changes\n\nThe reported release passed its validation jobs, then GitHub rejected the version commit with `fatal error in commit_refs_rules`. Successful security runs also contained high-severity CodeQL findings, while runtime guards, incomplete syntax discovery, obsolete dependencies and missing evidence checks could conceal failures.\n\n- Retry transient push failures three times without changing the commit; keep permanent rule refusals actionable and attest release metadata against the validated parent before every push. Preserve locked dependencies during versioning and remove downloaded helper evaluation.\n- Fix all five regex paths identified by the saved SARIF: PuTTY headers, booking references, tickets, visas and postal addresses. Keep finite subprocess regression probes with time and heap bounds.\n- Bring the entire shared pipeline up to date against both template trees: strict SARIF/audit/artifact gates, explicit runtime skips, frozen Deno preparation, dependency hook policy, safe artifact transport and Pages deployment, scheduled links, runner-acquisition recovery, shell lint and writer queues. Preserve the product APIs, session-publication corpus, 15 runtime/OS/shard legs and existing example platforms.\n- Add a patch changeset for the automatic release workflow.\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\nThe captured push response fails the original helper; mocked regressions verify recovery, bounded exhaustion and permanent-policy refusal. The original PuTTY and postal-address implementations exceed finite two-second subprocess bounds. Normal credential/address fixtures verify preserved matching behavior after the regex fixes.\n\nFocused automated checks cover push recovery, regex behavior, security evidence parsing, offline version/lock integrity, runtime skip visibility, artifact transport, workflow conditions and execution budgets. Full runtime, packaging, workflow, security and link verification runs in this PR's CI; the evidence report records exact SHAs and conclusions as verification completes.\n\n[Complete analysis, timeline, 24 findings and requirement mapping](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/blob/issue-92-255abc3c67f8/dev/log/issues/92/pulls/93/ANALYSIS.md). The same folder contains complete compressed historical logs, numbered annotations, repository/API responses, full template snapshots, bidirectional file inventories, research and before/after regression logs. [Template comparison](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/blob/issue-92-255abc3c67f8/dev/log/issues/92/pulls/93/research/TEMPLATE-COMPARISON.md).\n\nShared release-push defects reported upstream: [JavaScript template #283](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/283), [Python template #136](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/136). GitHub's internal server cause cannot be established from client logs; push classification diagnostics are available through `CI_SCRIPTS_DEBUG=1`, off by default. Live npm publishing remains restricted to main.\n\nFixes #92\n","headRefName":"issue-92-255abc3c67f8","isDraft":true,"mergeStateStatus":"UNSTABLE","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","conclusion":"","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/actions/runs/42077850614/job/127422724667","name":"Build web app","startedAt":"2026-11-05T17:46:33Z","status":"IN_PROGRESS","workflowName":"Example app"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","conclusion":"","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/actions/runs/42077850708/job/127422725340","name":"CodeQL (javascript-typescript)","startedAt":"2026-11-05T17:46:28Z","status":"IN_PROGRESS","workflowName":"Security"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-05T17:46:31Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","de